# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD (/opt/start.sh) boots the vulnerable Confluence
# broken-access-control sim on 0.0.0.0:8090 in the BACKGROUND and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so the unauthenticated /setup/setupadministrator.action
# privilege-escalation surface is ALREADY REACHABLE when the agent starts, and
# PID 1 is the sleep.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix flips ENFORCE_SETUP_ACCESS_CONTROL to True
# in /opt/confluence/app.py (or an equivalent access-control fix) and RESTARTS
# the sim. A fix written but never restarted leaves the running process on the
# old vulnerable code — still exploitable.
